+# Post-job cleanup · v7.0.72
+
+## Why
+
+v7.0.71 had cleanup only as whole-job deletion (Manage saved jobs & clips), which also deletes the final video. Nothing removed media that a finished video no longer needs. Two kinds of folder grew without limit:
+
+- **Generation jobs:** every Flow take (including unused takes), raw downloads, storyboard frames, references, narration and audio, stock copies, and any intermediate renders.
+- **Clip studio folders:** `_clip_work/<source>/` kept the downloaded source video and per-batch speech and frame files after each run finished.
+
+v7.0.72 adds a reviewed "Free space" step that keeps the finished video and removes only the media.
+
+## What is kept
+
+- Every validated final video in `render/` (`*final*.mp4`), and every finished clip output in a clip folder.
+- All JSON, text, subtitles, logs, reports, and Flow request journals (`*.flow-request.json`).
+- Symlinks, which are never followed or removed.
+
+## What is removed
+
+- **Generation job:** media files under the job folder (`.mp4`, `.mov`, `.jpg`, `.png`, `.mp3`, `.wav`, `.m4a`, and similar), plus any interrupted `render/.bounded-*` temp folders.
+- **Clip folder:** media files under `_clip_work/` (the downloaded source and batch work).
+
+Remote Google Flow media is never touched. Use the existing storage manager for that.
+
+## When it is blocked
+
+Nothing is deleted if any of these is true:
+
+- The job status is not `done`.
+- No final video in `render/` passes validation.
+- A Flow request is not `downloaded`.
+- `auto_resume.json` or `pause_state.json` shows an automatic resume that is running or waiting.
+- Production holds the job's `.production.lock`.
+- A clip run has no readable `highlights.json`.
+
+## How to use it (after the video is finished)
+
+1. Open the dashboard and go to **Manage saved jobs & clips**.
+2. Select the finished job or clip folder.
+3. Open **Free space after finishing**, then press **Review cleanup**.
+4. Check the category table and the kept video list.
+5. Tick the confirmation box, then press **Free space now**.
+
+The apply step recomputes the plan and refuses if anything changed since review.
+
+From the command line:
+
+```
+python3 cli.py v3 cleanup-plan <job_id>                 # preview, prints a digest
+python3 cli.py v3 cleanup-apply <job_id> --digest <d>   # delete exactly the reviewed set
+python3 cli.py v3 cleanup-plan --clip-folder <folder>
+python3 cli.py v3 cleanup-apply --clip-folder <folder> --digest <d>
+```
+
+Each applied cleanup writes `logs/post_job_cleanup_<time>.json` (clip folders: at the folder root) with the removed categories, bytes freed, and kept videos.
+
+## Trade-offs
+
+- After cleanup, source takes and narration cannot be used to re-render the job. Re-rendering a job would need new generation, which spends credits. Keep the final video.
+- A clip folder's source video must be downloaded again before its clips can be re-cut.
+- Cleanup is manual. Nothing is deleted automatically.
+
+## Not covered yet
+
+- Automatic cleanup on a schedule.
+- Remote Flow gallery cleanup (use the existing storage manager, which requires its own confirmation).
+- Live browser test of the Streamlit panel. The logic is covered by unit tests; please check the panel on your machine.
+
+## Install
+
+Stop the dashboard, then from the 7.0.71 installation folder:
+
+```
+python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.72/tools/update_v771_to_v772.py .            # dry run
+python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.72/tools/update_v771_to_v772.py . --apply
+```
+
+The updater replaces code and documentation only. Outputs, saved jobs, browser profiles, music, characters, and channel profiles are never copied, moved, or deleted.
